From: Custom Raumfeld firmware project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs4271: recognize the current mute pin binding

The YAML binding uses amuteb-eq-bmutec, while the driver still reads the
legacy amutec-eq-bmutec spelling. Accept the binding and keep compatibility
with older device trees. Connector 2 relies on the vendor mute pin setting.

Signed-off-by: Custom Raumfeld firmware project
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs4271.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs4271.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs4271.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs4271.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs4271.c
@@ -596,7 +596,9 @@ static int cs4271_component_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	bool amutec_eq_bmutec;
 
 	amutec_eq_bmutec = of_property_read_bool(component->dev->of_node,
-						 "cirrus,amutec-eq-bmutec");
+						 "cirrus,amuteb-eq-bmutec") ||
+			  of_property_read_bool(component->dev->of_node,
+						 "cirrus,amutec-eq-bmutec");
 	cs4271->enable_soft_reset = of_property_read_bool(component->dev->of_node,
 							  "cirrus,enable-soft-reset");
 
